          "type": "text",
          "title": "Ingestion trace notes",
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 12,
            "w": 24,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 81
          },
          "options": {
            "mode": "markdown",
            "content": "Span layout, outermost first:\n\n- `jsrpc` / `queue` / `scheduled` — Cloudflare's root span, named after the trigger. `jsrpc` is the API calling ingestion over the service binding (the fast path), `queue` is the durable backstop, `scheduled` is the redrive cron.\n- `ingestion.job_total` — one claimed job.\n- `ingestion.source_total` — one source inside that job. Batched resume means a large source can span several invocations, so job and source spans do not always nest one-to-one.\n- `ingestion_stage.*` — the pipeline stages. Each carries `crosmos.stage`, `crosmos.outcome`, and where relevant `crosmos.input_count` / `crosmos.output_count` / `crosmos.chunks_processed` / `crosmos.attempt`.\n\nUseful TraceQL:\n\n| Want | Query |\n| --- | --- |\n| Ingestion only, per source | `{ name = \"ingestion.source_total\" }` |\n| Slow sources | `{ name = \"ingestion.source_total\" && duration > 10s }` |\n| Failures anywhere in ingestion | `{ resource.service.name = \"crosmos-ingestion-production\" && span.crosmos.outcome = \"failed\" }` |\n| One stage across all jobs | `{ span.crosmos.stage = \"memory_extraction\" }` |\n| Big sources | `{ span.crosmos.chunks_processed > 8 }` |\n| Extraction model calls | `{ name = \"fetch\" && span.url.path = \"/v1/chat/completions\" }` |\n\nWhen the API enqueues over the RPC binding, a single trace contains both `crosmos-api-production` and `crosmos-ingestion-production` spans, so the waterfall shows submit-to-persist in one view. Queue-triggered retries arrive as their own `queue`-rooted trace; correlate those with the API request through `request_id` and the job/source IDs in structured logs.\n\nTwo caveats. TraceQL **metric** panels are capped at a 25-hour window by Grafana Cloud, so this dashboard defaults to 6h; trace search tables have no such cap. And at current traffic the quantile panels are computed from an exponential histogram, so values snap to bucket boundaries (0.13s, 0.27s, 0.54s, 1.07s, 2.15s, 4.29s, 8.59s) — read them as ranges and use the trace tables when you need an exact duration."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
